				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-19258da4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="19258da4" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h2 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Marketing for a specialty <span class="hl">that's genuinely two businesses in one</span></h2>				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-62d30f7e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="62d30f7e" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2550d3a0 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="2550d3a0" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-410d1332 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="410d1332" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>Dermatology occupies a category almost no other clinic type does: acne and eczema patients, medically motivated and sometimes using insurance, and injectables and laser patients, self-pay and aesthetically motivated — walking through the exact same door. Marketing built for only one side misses the other&#8217;s revenue and search demand entirely. And because it&#8217;s doctor-led, a dermatology clinic is marketed differently from a facial-led <a href="/skin-care-clinics/">skin care clinic</a> or an injectables-focused <a href="/aesthetic-clinics/">aesthetic clinic</a>: the dermatologist&#8217;s credentials are the centre of the story.</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-59818f45 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="59818f45" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Specialist referral networks are a real channel, not an afterthought</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-51bd429c elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="51bd429c" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>Many dermatology patients arrive via GP referral, not a Google search — which makes LinkedIn relationship-building with referring doctors, corporate HR contacts and insurance coordinators a genuine, underused marketing channel most beauty-focused agencies never touch.</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-1842a283 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="1842a283" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Missed calls are a quiet, expensive leak</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-6f930a18 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="6f930a18" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>Busy front desks miss calls — across salons and spas, Zenoti&#8217;s 2025 industry data found 37% of calls go unanswered <small>(Source: Zenoti, 2025)</small>. At a dermatology clinic&#8217;s per-patient value, that&#8217;s real monthly revenue disappearing before anyone picks up. Our <a href="/ai-appointment-booking-bot/">AI receptionist for clinics</a> answers every enquiry, day or night, and books the consultation.</p>								</div>
				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-1c40b905 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="1c40b905" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container" data-settings="{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7b27f12e elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="7b27f12e" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:19px;color:#fff;margin:0 0 10px">Dermatology clinics, at a glance</p><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);font-size:14px;color:#D9D5E4"><b style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;color:#C6F432;min-width:120px">Dual nature</b><span>— medical and aesthetic, marketed differently</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);font-size:14px;color:#D9D5E4"><b style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;color:#C6F432;min-width:120px">37%</b><span>of calls to salons &amp; spas go unanswered (Source: Zenoti, 2025)</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);font-size:14px;color:#D9D5E4"><b style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;color:#C6F432;min-width:120px">Days to weeks</b><span>of research before many patients book</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);font-size:14px;color:#D9D5E4"><b style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;color:#C6F432;min-width:120px">Referrals</b><span>are a real channel — GPs, insurers, corporates</span></div>								</div>
				</div>
